# Phase 7: Project Documentation

## Project Title

EduGenie: Google Gemini Powered Learning Assistant

## 1. Project Overview

EduGenie is an AI-powered educational web application developed to help students learn and understand academic topics.

The application uses Google Gemini for Generative AI responses and FastAPI for backend processing.

## 2. Objectives

The main objectives are:

- Provide AI-powered academic assistance.
- Explain difficult topics simply.
- Generate quizzes.
- Generate summaries.
- Provide learning paths.
- Provide all features through one simple interface.

## 3. Technologies

- Python
- FastAPI
- Google Gemini
- HTML
- CSS
- Jinja2
- Uvicorn
- GitHub
- Render

## 4. Main Features

### Q&A

Provides answers to student questions.

### Explain

Provides simple explanations.

### Quiz

Generates multiple-choice questions.

### Summary

Provides short summaries.

### Learning Path

Provides structured learning levels.

## 5. Backend

FastAPI handles:

- Routing
- Form data
- User input
- Gemini requests
- Response generation
- HTML rendering

## 6. Frontend

HTML provides the application structure.

CSS provides the visual styling.

Jinja2 is used to display dynamic data from the backend.

## 7. AI Integration

Google Gemini processes the prompts generated by the backend and produces educational responses.

The Gemini API key is stored securely as an environment variable.

## 8. Workflow

User
→ Select Task
→ Enter Topic/Question
→ FastAPI
→ Google Gemini
→ AI Response
→ Response Page

## 9. Deployment

The application is deployed using Render.

